// codebox_pass.gen -- f_ks stage 0b: holds last frame's state u, or reseeds it. 256x256 float32.
// Mirror: tests/modules/ks/ks_mirror.seed_state() (seeding); identity otherwise.
//
// Inputs: the first inlet is the `r draw` bang (unused; it only triggers the render every frame, and the
// feedback arrives on a cold inlet so it cannot retrigger the loop), the second is the feedback state
// (R = u, from the nl stage through the hold stage), the third is the noise texture (R in [0,1), from
// the seed stage).
// reseed = 1 replaces the state with (2*noise - 1) * amp: uniform in [-amp, amp], never zero (u = 0 is a
// fixed point, FR-003). reseed fires on load and on the reset trigger (FR-007).
//   - SELF-HEAL: a texel of the feedback that is exactly 0 is reseeded from the noise too. A live KS
//     field never holds an exact 0 (float32 values), so this fires only when the state was lost: a
//     fresh module, a GL context rebuilt by a window mode change (floating <-> fullscreen), or a
//     non-finite texel the nl stage zapped to 0. u = 0 everywhere is a fixed point, so without this a
//     lost state stays flat grey forever
//   - selection uses switch(), not mix(): mix(NaN, x, 1) is still NaN, so a poisoned feedback
//     texel could survive a reseed through mix
//   - the feedback is NaN/Inf-guarded: abs(x) < 1e30 (NaN == NaN is TRUE on this GPU)
Param reseed(0);
Param amp(1);

fb = nearest(in2, norm).x;
fb = switch(abs(fb) < 1e30, fb, 0);
nz = (nearest(in3, norm).x * 2 - 1) * amp;
kept = switch(fb == 0, nz, fb);
out1 = vec(switch(reseed >= 0.5, nz, kept), 0, 0, 1);
